# makes no image, so that half belongs to container/Dockerfile, where
# apps/generic/tests/dockercli runs /backupd inside the built image.
#
# Their harness needed one fix that is worth knowing about here, because this
# repository caused it. `docker cp` copies a symlink AS a symlink, and the new
# image ships /backupd with /backupd as a link to it, so extraction was
# landing a four-byte dangling link and exec'ing it. They pass `-L` now, which
# is a no-op against a pre-rename image. The same defect was in this
# repository's own release scripts and is fixed on the image branch.
